": "engenn5le07ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to float along"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move slowly through something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: John is just floating along in his life on the ship."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about your job."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to wrap up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to complete a task; to conclude an event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter wrapped up a project at work last week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "passenger"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who pays to ride on public transportation, such as a bus, a ship or an airplane"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: John plans activities for passengers on the ship."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "presentation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an activity where someone shows or explains something to a group of people "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Staff often give presentations to others for them to learn new things."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pass with flying colors"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to pass a test with a good score"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I really hope I pass this test with flying colors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "recruiter"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who finds suitable individuals to join a company"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Recruiters look for people with good grades."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "high-paying"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a job that pays a high salary"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If Peter gets a high-paying job, he will go on a cruise next year."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the First Conditional to talk about real possibilities in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will do something. In that condition, something else will happen."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If clause \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Clause \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If you cook the meat too long,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it will burn.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible you will cook the meat too long. In this condition: it will burn.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If I ask the teacher to help me,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I will pass the test. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible I will ask the t